Index: Security

Purpose:
  Security control layer entry point. Security is a cross-cutting concern
  that applies to every stage of the SDLC, not a single stage or skill.
  This index routes to the security policy, controls, gates, threats,
  and scanners.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
  1  INDEX.sdd (this file)
  2  levels.sdd (security level definitions L0-L5)
  3  SECURITY.sdd (security policy and scope)
  4  controls.sdd (security controls catalog)
  5  gates.sdd (security gates overview)
  6  gates/ (individual gate specifications)
  7  threats.sdd (threat model)
  8  scanners.sdd (security scanners and their configuration)
  9  findings/ (security findings, when applicable)

Modes:
  APPLY   — apply security controls to a task/chain
  AUDIT   — audit security posture
  SCAN    — run security scanners
  GATE    — evaluate security gate pass/fail

Rules:
  [SEC1]  AI MUST load this index before reading any security file.
  [SEC2]  Security is mandatory for all changes — AI MUST NOT skip
          security applicability calculation.
  [SEC3]  Security controls are selected based on risk level (R0-R5),
          not applied uniformly.
  [SEC4]  Critical and High findings MUST block VR until resolved.
          Only human MAY accept an unresolved Critical/High finding.
  [SEC5]  Security exceptions MUST be recorded explicitly with owner,
          reason, and expiration date.
  [SEC6]  Security review level is determined by project SecurityLevel
          (L0-L5), not by individual preference.
  [SEC7]  DDoS, pentest, and other heavy controls are triggered by
          conditions, not applied to every change.
  [SEC8]  Security findings MUST have a lifecycle: ~ ? triaged ?
          task-created ? fixing ? verification ? + (or x for false
          positive, @ for accepted risk).
  [SEC9]  Security layer coordinates with chains/chains.sdd -> SecurityGate,
          tasks/tasks.sdd -> SecurityAcceptanceCriteria/SecuritySeverity,
          and project/project.sdd -> SecurityRiskBudget.
  [SEC10] Security MUST NOT be treated as a final-stage checkbox.
          It is a continuous control layer throughout the SDLC.


SecurityLevels:
  L0: baseline (no additional controls)
  L1: baseline + automated scans
  L2: scans + security tests
  L3: threat model + DAST
  L4: pentest + architecture security review
  L5: continuous security + external assessment


